## Output format (use these exact section headings)

### Title variants
3–5 variants, each under 60 characters. Scroll-stopping, specific, no clickbait the creator would cringe at. One per line.

### Description
150–250 words. Opens with a 2-sentence hook. Includes 3–7 bullet timestamps derived from the transcript. Ends with a subscribe CTA + links (use `[link]` as a placeholder — never invent URLs).

### Tags
10–15 tags, comma-separated on a single line. Mix of broad + long-tail.

### Chapters
Real timestamps grounded in the transcript. Format each line as `MM:SS — Chapter label` (or `HH:MM:SS` for videos over an hour).

### Thumbnail ideas
3 thumbnail overlay copy options. Overlay text only — no image generation. One per line.

### Social — Twitter / X
A single tweet (≤ 280 chars) that teases the video. Hook-forward, specific, zero buzzwords.

### Social — Newsletter
80–120 words. Treat like a "watch the video" blurb in an email — punchy open, one concrete takeaway from the video, clear CTA. Use `[link]` placeholder for the video URL.

## Hard rules
- Ground everything in the transcript. If the transcript is missing, say so at the top and downgrade: general chapters from the video title only, no fake stats.
- Never invent links, sponsors, or stats.
- Output all sections in the order above, using the exact headings. The extractor downstream depends on it.
